From: INMYS <support@inmys.ru>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: pwm: elvees: describe dual-output mode

Describe the optional fixed eight-output interface and shared periods.
Retain the existing four-output interface by default. Also list the
compatible used by the driver and the binding example.

Signed-off-by: INMYS <support@inmys.ru>
---
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pwm/pwm-elvees.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pwm/pwm-elvees.yaml
@@ -12,14 +12,18 @@
 description: |+
   Bindings for the ELVEES PWM controller.
 
-  ELVEES PWM controller supports 4 channels and only one output for
-  each channel.
+  ELVEES PWM controller supports 4 timers with two outputs each.
+  By default, one output per timer is exposed. With elvees,dual-output,
+  PWM indices 0..3 select OUTA0..3 and 4..7 select OUTB0..3.
+  Outputs A and B of each timer share their period, but have independent
+  duty cycles. Conflicting periods on enabled outputs are rejected.
 
 
 properties:
   compatible:
     enum:
       - elvees,mcom-pwm
+      - elvees,elvees-pwm
 
   "#pwm-cells":
     const: 2
@@ -29,6 +33,13 @@
 
   clocks:
     maxItems: 1
+
+  elvees,dual-output:
+    type: boolean
+    description: |
+      Expose all eight outputs with fixed numbering as described above.
+      elvees,output-channel and elvees,state-on-disable are ignored in this
+      mode. Disabled outputs are driven to the inactive polarity level.
 
   elvees,output-channel:
     description: |+
